    "https://jobs.sunderland.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=0327-26": {
      "title": "Research and Innovation Operations Manager",
      "description": "0327-26 Research and Innovation Operations Manager - 6 month secondment - Jobs at the University of Sunderland Skip to main content University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Terms of Use Contact Us Cookie Information Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Research and Innovation Operations Manager - 6 month secondment Go to The University of Sunderland Close menu University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Close Search Search Search Please note: this vacancy is only available to current employees of the University Further details: Job Description Your next opportunity This six-month secondment offers an exciting opportunity to provide operational leadership to the Research and Innovation service during a period of transformation. Working closely with the Pro Vice-Chancellor Research and Innovation, the postholder will play a key role in strengthening team performance, improving processes and governance, embedding new ways of working, and supporting the development of a revised service structure. The role is ideally suited to an experienced manager who can bring clarity, coordination and pace to operational delivery, enabling the team to work effectively and focus on achieving its strategic objectives. Is this you? You will bring operational management experience, alongside a proven ability to support continuous improvement and organisational change initiatives. Skilled in building effective partnerships, you will have experience of working collaboratively with external service providers and stakeholders, including those in international or transnational settings. You will be highly organised, with the ability to manage competing priorities and deliver results in a fast-paced environment. An excellent communicator with strong written, verbal and presentation skills, you will be confident in developing positive relationships and influencing a wide range of stakeholders at all levels, both within and beyond the University. Adaptable, collaborative and solutions-focused, you will work flexibly with others to achieve shared goals and deliver high-quality outcomes. Ready to Apply? Before getting started, please download the Role Profile under ‘Job Description’ so you have everything you need. Our application questions assess you directly against the essential and desirable criteria for the role. We do not review CVs at this stage, so please provide detailed, evidence-based answers to help us understand your suitability. Closing date: Sunday 13 September (23:59 GMT) Email details to a friend Apply Online View All Vacancies Job Details Department Research & Global Engagement - Research Location Sunderland Campus Salary £58,997 to £67,466 Hours per Week 37 Closing Date Sunday 13 September 2026 Interview Date Wednesday 23 September 2026 Reference 0327-26 Apply Online Current Vacancies Sunderland Vacancies Graduate Internships London Vacancies Overseas Vacancies Partner Organisations Student/Graduate Opportunities Find Jobs Jobs by Email Search Jobs: Search Advanced Search Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookie Information | Accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.sunderland.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=0254-26": {
      "title": "Research Data and Infrastructure Engineer",
      "description": "0254-26 Research Data and Infrastructure Engineer - Jobs at the University of Sunderland Skip to main content University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Terms of Use Contact Us Cookie Information Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Research Data and Infrastructure Engineer Go to The University of Sunderland Close menu University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Close Search Search Search Further details: Job Description Proud to be Sunderland The University of Sunderland offers life‑changing opportunities for more than 27,500 students across our campuses in Sunderland, London and Hong Kong, as well as through global partnerships in 19 countries. We’re an inclusive, ambitious and forward‑looking University in a vibrant city that’s constantly evolving. We’re also entering an exciting new phase with a refreshed vision and strategic ambitions shaped around the changing higher education landscape. As we move through 2026, we’re celebrating being recognised as: A top 30 UK university (Guardian University Guide 2026) 1st in the North ‑ East for student support services (Daily Mail University Guide 2026) 1st in the North ‑ East for teaching quality (The Times & Sunday Times Good University Guide 2026) Your next opportunity Help build the future of AI-enabled healthcare. The Northern Ophthalmic Research and Innovation (NORI) Institute is an ambitious partnership between the Universities of Sunderland, Durham, and Newcastle, South Tyneside and Sunderland NHS Foundation Trust, and a network of national and international partners. Our mission is to transform how health and disease are detected, understood, and managed through the integration of advanced analytics, multimodal health data, retinal imaging, artificial intelligence, and real-world clinical innovation. We are seeking an exceptional Research Data and Infrastructure Engineer to play a leading role in designing and delivering the secure research data infrastructure that underpins this vision. This is a rare opportunity to help shape a nationally significant research platform from the ground up, developing cloud-native environments, scalable analytics pipelines, and secure data services that support cutting-edge research and the deployment of data-driven technologies into healthcare. Working across university, NHS, civic, and industry partners, you will lead the development of secure cloud infrastructure, integrate complex healthcare and research datasets across multiple systems and Secure Data Environments, and enable researchers, clinicians, and innovators to work safely with large-scale multimodal data. Your work will directly support the development of new diagnostic approaches, AI-enabled technologies, and translational research programmes designed to improve patient outcomes and reduce health inequalities. We are looking for a highly motivated engineer with expertise in cloud platforms, data engineering, infrastructure automation, and secure analytics environments. Whether your experience comes from healthcare, research, technology, or other data-intensive sectors, you will be excited by the opportunity to solve complex technical challenges, work with multidisciplinary teams, and contribute to infrastructure that delivers real-world impact at scale. If you want to help build the next generation of trusted health data infrastructure and play a key role in one of the UK’s most exciting emerging research and innovation programmes, we would love to hear from you. NORI's vision is supported by INSIGHT - the Eye and Oculomics Health Data Research Hub at Moorfields Eye Hospital NHS Foundation Trust (https://www.insight.hdrhub.org/). INSIGHT is the world's largest ophthalmic bio-resource, with over 30 million eye images linked to clinical data. The Hub's core mission is to reduce the burden of blindness by providing safe and trusted research access to large scale ophthalmic data. INSIGHT provides leadership across data research governance (including patient/public engagement) data curation, cloud-based research infrastructure and artificial medical intelligence. In 2025, INSIGHT at Moorfields was awarded major grant funding by the MRC to enhance and expand INSIGHT to other NHS Trusts and health datasets with the aim of transforming UK eye health research by connecting national data resources to accelerate discovery and contribute to improved clinical outcomes for the benefit of patients and wider society. The Research Data and Infrastructure Engineer role is co-funded by this MRC grant award, and the role will support NORI leadership to integrate and onboard Sunderland Specialist Eye Hospital as a data collection centre with INSIGHT. Please note this is a fixed-term post for 3 years. Is this you? 1. Technical Leadership in Secure Research Data Platforms Extensive experience leading the design, implementation and operational management of secure, cloud-based research data platforms and engineering solutions within complex production or research environments. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong track record of architecting scalable data infrastructure, implementing modern software engineering and Infrastructure-as-Code practices, and delivering reliable, resilient and maintainable data platforms. They should be capable of providing technical leadership across the full engineering lifecycle, from architecture and implementation through to operational optimisation and continuous improvement. What we’re looking for: * Leadership of cloud-native research or enterprise data platforms. * Strong data engineering and software engineering capability. * Experience delivering production-grade infrastructure at scale. * Evidence of technical ownership rather than simply contributing to projects. 2. Secure Health Data Engineering, Governance and Interoperability Significant experience engineering and managing sensitive healthcare or research data within highly regulated environments, ensuring robust governance, interoperability, security and compliance. Candidates must demonstrate experience of working within secure research or NHS environments, balancing innovation with the requirements of information governance, privacy, cyber security and regulatory compliance. They should understand federated data architectures, secure data environments and the practical implementation of reproducible, auditable and trusted research infrastructure. What we’re looking for: * Experience with NHS, healthcare or similarly regulated data environments. * Knowledge of Secure Data Environments, UK GDPR and information governance. * Ability to integrate data securely across multiple systems and organisations. * Demonstrable understanding of governance-by-design. 3. Translational Research Infrastructure and Partnership Working Proven ability to translate complex research and clinical requirements into operational technical solutions while working effectively across multidisciplinary partnerships. This role extends beyond engineering. The successful candidate will be able to engage confidently with researchers, clinicians, digital teams and external partners, translating research objectives into scalable technical solutions that enable AI, advanced analytics and real-world clinical innovation. They will demonstrate excellent communication skills, sound technical judgement and the ability to influence infrastructure strategy across organisational boundaries. What we’re looking for: * Experience working across academia, healthcare and technical teams. * Ability to bridge research, engineering and operational delivery. * Strong stakeholder management and communication skills. * Evidence of delivering infrastructure that supports translational research and AI-enabled innovation. Why join us? At the University of Sunderland, we’re more than a place of learning, we’re a welcoming community that values inclusivity, collaboration, and well-being. We don’t just offer jobs, we offer careers that come with support, flexibility, and plenty of perks: Up to 49 days’ holiday - that’s 36 days’ annual leave, 5 festive closure days and 8 Bank Holidays! Award-winning staff networks that celebrate who you are. Lifestyle benefits , with savings on shopping, tech, bikes, and even cars. Health and well-being support , from private medical cover to gym discounts. Learning and development that helps you achieve your goals. Ready to Apply? Before getting started, please download the Role Profile under ‘Job Description’ so you have everything you need. Our application questions assess you directly against the essential and desirable criteria for the role. We do not review CVs at this stage, so please provide detailed, evidence-based answers to help us understand your suitability. Closing date: Sunday 13 th September (23:59 GMT) If you have questions about the role, please contact: Professor Matthew Campbell - mathew.campbell@sunderland.ac.uk Head and Co-Director of NORI, and Interim PVC for the Faculty of Health Sciences and Wellbeing. We may close this vacancy earlier than the advertised closing date if we receive a high volume of applications. If this sounds like the opportunity for you, don't wait – get your application in early! Email details to a friend Apply Online Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Department Health Sciences & Wellbeing - Executive (FHSW) Location Sunderland Campus Salary £46,756 to £58,228 Hours per Week 37 Closing Date Sunday 13 September 2026 Interview Date To be confirmed Reference 0254-26 Apply Online Current Vacancies Sunderland Vacancies Graduate Internships London Vacancies Overseas Vacancies Partner Organisations Student/Graduate Opportunities Find Jobs Jobs by Email Search Jobs: Search Advanced Search Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookie Information | Accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.sunderland.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=0326-26": {
      "title": "Research Funding Manager",
      "description": "0326-26 Research Funding Manager - Jobs at the University of Sunderland Skip to main content University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Terms of Use Contact Us Cookie Information Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Research Funding Manager Go to The University of Sunderland Close menu University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Close Search Search Search Further details: Job Description Proud to be Sunderland The University of Sunderland offers life‑changing opportunities for more than 27,500 students across our campuses in Sunderland, London and Hong Kong, as well as through global partnerships in 19 countries. We’re an inclusive, ambitious and forward‑looking University in a vibrant city that’s constantly evolving. We’re also entering an exciting new phase with a refreshed vision and strategic ambitions shaped around the changing higher education landscape. As we move through 2026, we’re celebrating being recognised as: A top 30 UK university (Guardian University Guide 2026) 1st in the North‑East for student support services (Daily Mail University Guide 2026) 1st in the North‑East for teaching quality (The Times & Sunday Times Good University Guide 2026) Your next opportunity As Research Funding Manager, you will lead the University’s research funding support function, providing expert guidance and strategic leadership to help academics secure external research funding. Working at the heart of Research and Innovation, you will use your in-depth knowledge of the UK and international funding landscape to identify opportunities, provide funder intelligence, and support the development of high-quality, competitive funding applications. You will lead a specialist team delivering end-to-end support across the research funding lifecycle, ensuring applications are well-coordinated, compliant and submitted successfully. Collaborating closely with academic colleagues and professional service teams, you will drive continuous improvement in processes, systems and service delivery, helping to increase research income, strengthen funding success rates and support the University’s research ambitions. Is this you? You will bring strong experience in research funding support, research development or research administration, along with a solid understanding of the UK research funding landscape and what it takes to develop successful funding applications. With experience of managing people, priorities and deadlines, you'll be confident leading and supporting a team while building positive relationships with academic colleagues and professional service partners across the University. You'll enjoy working collaboratively, helping researchers navigate funding opportunities and delivering a high-quality service that makes a real difference. You will have excellent communication, organisational and analytical skills, enabling you to turn complex funder requirements into clear, practical advice. You'll be comfortable using data and insights to inform decision-making, identify opportunities for improvement and help shape efficient and effective research funding processes. Most importantly, you'll be a proactive, approachable and service-focused professional who is passionate about supporting researchers to achieve funding success and helping to grow the University's research ambitions. Why join us? At the University of Sunderland, we’re more than a place of learning, we’re a welcoming community that values inclusivity, collaboration, and well-being. We don’t just offer jobs, we offer careers that come with support, flexibility, and plenty of perks: Up to 49 days’ holiday - that’s 36 days’ annual leave, 5 festive closure days and 8 Bank Holidays! Award-winning staff networks that celebrate who you are. Lifestyle benefits , with savings on shopping, tech, bikes, and even cars. Health and well-being support , from private medical cover to gym discounts. Learning and development that helps you achieve your goals. Ready to Apply? Before getting started, please download the Role Profile under ‘Job Description’ so you have everything you need. Our application questions assess you directly against the essential and desirable criteria for the role. We do not review CVs at this stage, so please provide detailed, evidence-based answers to help us understand your suitability. Closing date: Sunday 13 September (23:59 GMT) Email details to a friend Apply Online Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Department Research & Global Engagement - Research Location Sunderland Campus Salary £46,756 to £58,228 Hours per Week 37 Closing Date Sunday 13 September 2026 Interview Date Friday 25 September 2026 Reference 0326-26 Apply Online Current Vacancies Sunderland Vacancies Graduate Internships London Vacancies Overseas Vacancies Partner Organisations Student/Graduate Opportunities Find Jobs Jobs by Email Search Jobs: Search Advanced Search Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookie Information | Accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.sunderland.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=0340-26": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer",
      "description": "0340-26 Senior Lecturer - Cardiac Physiology - Jobs at the University of Sunderland Skip to main content University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Terms of Use Contact Us Cookie Information Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Senior Lecturer - Cardiac Physiology Go to The University of Sunderland Close menu University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Close Search Search Search Please note: this vacancy is only available to current employees of the University Further details: Job Description Your next opportunity We are seeking an ambitious, enthusiastic and student-centred Senior Lecturer in Cardiac Physiology to deliver an outstanding academic experience across our BSc (Hons) Cardiac Physiology and BSc (Hons) Cardiac Physiology Practice Degree Apprenticeship programmes, as well as supporting future programme development. You will contribute to teaching and learning across undergraduate Cardiac Physiology, Healthcare Science and other health-related programmes within the Faculty. Teaching delivery will take place on campus, within practice settings and online, providing students with an engaging and inclusive learning experience. The role also offers the opportunity to contribute to the University's growing research and knowledge exchange agenda. You will be encouraged to develop research activity, build external partnerships and strengthen the national and international profile of the department. The University is committed to supporting your continued professional and academic development and offers a Postgraduate Certificate in Learning and Teaching in Higher Education leading to HEA accreditation for those who do not already hold a teaching qualification. Is this you? You will be an experienced Cardiac Physiologist with a strong commitment to educating and inspiring the next generation of healthcare professionals. As a Senior Lecturer, you will demonstrate professional expertise alongside substantial teaching and learning experience within higher education, clinical practice, or both. We are looking for someone with excellent leadership, organisational, interpersonal and communication skills, together with a thorough understanding of healthcare science, research and evidence-informed, sustainable practice. You will be able to articulate a clear vision for research and knowledge exchange activities, demonstrate a commitment to employability and continuing professional development, and contribute positively to academic leadership within the Faculty. Applications are welcomed from HCPC-registered Cardiac Physiologists or those registered with the Academy for Healthcare Science who are passionate about shaping the future of Cardiac Physiology education and practice. Why join us? At the University of Sunderland, we’re more than a place of learning, we’re a welcoming community that values inclusivity, collaboration, and well-being. We don’t just offer jobs, we offer careers that come with support, flexibility, and plenty of perks: Up to 49 days’ holiday - that’s 36 days’ annual leave, 5 festive closure days and 8 Bank Holidays! Award-winning staff networks that celebrate who you are. Lifestyle benefits, with savings on shopping, tech, bikes, and even cars. Health and well-being support, from private medical cover to gym discounts. Learning and development that helps you achieve your goals. Ready to Apply? Before getting started, please download the Role Profile under ‘Job Description’ so you have everything you need. Our application questions assess you directly against the essential and desirable criteria for the role. We do not review CVs at this stage, so please provide detailed, evidence-based answers to help us understand your suitability. Closing date: Monday 7 September (23:59 GMT) If you have any questions about this role, please contact - Christopher Cox - Associate Head of School for Biosciences c.cox@sunderland.ac.uk Email details to a friend Apply Online View All Vacancies Job Details Department Health Sciences & Wellbeing - School of Pharmacy & Pharmaceutical Sciences Location Sunderland Campus Salary £46,756 to £58,228 Hours per Week 37 Closing Date Monday 07 September 2026 Reference 0340-26 Apply Online Current Vacancies Sunderland Vacancies Graduate Internships London Vacancies Overseas Vacancies Partner Organisations Student/Graduate Opportunities Find Jobs Jobs by Email Search Jobs: Search Advanced Search Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookie Information | Accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.sunderland.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=0328-26": {
      "title": "Investigation Committee Chair",
      "description": "0328-26 Investigation Committee Chair - Jobs at the University of Sunderland Skip to main content University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Terms of Use Contact Us Cookie Information Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Investigation Committee Chair Go to The University of Sunderland Close menu University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Close Search Search Search Further details: Job Description Proud to be Sunderland The University of Sunderland offers life‑changing opportunities for more than 27,500 students across our campuses in Sunderland, London and Hong Kong, as well as through global partnerships in 19 countries. We’re an inclusive, ambitious and forward‑looking University in a vibrant city that’s constantly evolving. We’re also entering an exciting new phase with a refreshed vision and strategic ambitions shaped around the changing higher education landscape. As we move through 2026, we’re celebrating being recognised as: A top 30 UK university (Guardian University Guide 2026) 1st in the North ‑ East for student support services (Daily Mail University Guide 2026) 1st in the North ‑ East for teaching quality (The Times & Sunday Times Good University Guide 2026) Your next opportunity Sunderland Medical School was one of only five new Medical Schools established to address the regional imbalance of medical education places across England and to widen access to ensure that the profession reflects the communities it serves. At full capacity we have a cohort of 585 Medical Students. The School of Medicine sits within the Faculty of Health Sciences and Wellbeing at Sunderland University which has a track-record of excellence in science and healthcare education spanning almost 100 years. Our programme allows medical students to learn within our state-of-the-art teaching and learning spaces, including outstanding laboratory facilities, the latest in high fidelity clinical simulation equipment and some of the best hospital, third sector and GP settings in England. Please note, this role will be paid on the Clinical Academic PayScale as appropriate. Is this you? The successful candidate will be a GMC-registered doctor with substantial experience of medical education and a strong understanding of Fitness to Practise processes. You will bring sound judgement, integrity, and the ability to make fair, transparent, and evidence-based decisions in complex and sensitive cases involving student conduct, professionalism, health, and patient safety. You will have experience working within the NHS and higher education environments and understand the governance arrangements that support medical student progression. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills are essential, as is the ability to engage effectively with students, academic colleagues, professional services teams, senior leaders, clinical partners, and regulators. Why join us? At the University of Sunderland, we’re more than a place of learning, we’re a welcoming community that values inclusivity, collaboration, and well-being. We don’t just offer jobs, we offer careers that come with support, flexibility, and plenty of perks: Up to 49 days’ holiday - that’s 36 days’ annual leave, 5 festive closure days and 8 Bank Holidays! Award-winning staff networks that celebrate who you are. Lifestyle benefits , with savings on shopping, tech, bikes, and even cars. Health and well-being support , from private medical cover to gym discounts. Learning and development that helps you achieve your goals. *Please note, holidays and salary are calculated on a pro rata basis. Ready to Apply? Before getting started, please download the Role Profile under ‘Job Description’ so you have everything you need. Our application questions assess you directly against the essential and desirable criteria for the role. We do not review CVs at this stage, so please provide detailed, evidence-based answers to help us understand your suitability. Closing date: Sunday 6th September 2026 (23:59 GMT) If you have questions about the role, please contact: Professor Mark Shipley, Undergraduate Programme Lead, Mark.Shipley@Sunderland.ac.uk We may close this vacancy earlier than the advertised closing date if we receive a high volume of applications. If this sounds like the opportunity for you, don't wait – get your application in early! Email details to a friend Apply Online Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Department Health Sciences & Wellbeing - School of Medicine Location Sunderland Campus Salary This role will be paid on the Clinical Academic PayScale as appropriate. Hours per Week 3.7 Closing Date Sunday 06 September 2026 Interview Date Wednesday 16 September 2026 Reference 0328-26 Apply Online Current Vacancies Sunderland Vacancies Graduate Internships London Vacancies Overseas Vacancies Partner Organisations Student/Graduate Opportunities Find Jobs Jobs by Email Search Jobs: Search Advanced Search Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookie Information | Accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.sunderland.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=0315-26": {
      "title": "Technical Solutions Analyst (12-month fixed term)",
      "description": "0315-26 Technical Solutions Analyst (12-month fixed term) - Jobs at the University of Sunderland Skip to main content University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Terms of Use Contact Us Cookie Information Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Technical Solutions Analyst (12-month fixed term) Go to The University of Sunderland Close menu University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Close Search Search Search Further details: Job Description Proud to be Sunderland The University of Sunderland offers life‑changing opportunities for more than 27,500 students across our campuses in Sunderland, London and Hong Kong, as well as through global partnerships in 19 countries. We’re an inclusive, ambitious and forward‑looking University in a vibrant city that’s constantly evolving. We’re also entering an exciting new phase with a refreshed vision and strategic ambitions shaped around the changing higher education landscape. As we move through 2026, we’re celebrating being recognised as: A top 30 UK university (Guardian University Guide 2026) 1st in the North‑East for student support services (Daily Mail University Guide 2026) 1st in the North‑East for teaching quality (The Times & Sunday Times Good University Guide 2026) Your next opportunity Join our Enterprise Architecture team and play a key role in shaping technology solutions that support the University's strategic ambitions. As a Technical Solutions Analyst, you will bridge the gap between business needs and technical delivery, analysing systems, applications, data and integrations to identify practical, sustainable solutions. Working closely with architects, technical specialists, project teams and operational colleagues, you will help translate complex requirements into clear recommendations, support technology change initiatives from discovery through to implementation, and ensure solutions are successfully transitioned into business-as-usual services. Please note this is a 12-month fixed term contract, with hybrid working, based on-site at Sunderland Campus. Is this you? You'll bring experience of analysing business and technical requirements and translating them into practical technology solutions within complex environments. With strong analytical and problem-solving skills, you'll be confident evaluating solution options, documenting systems and integrations, and identifying risks, dependencies and implementation considerations. You'll be able to communicate complex technical concepts clearly to both technical and non-technical stakeholders, produce high-quality documentation, and work collaboratively to deliver successful technology change. Experience of enterprise and cloud technologies, including Microsoft Azure, Microsoft 365, Power Platform and Dynamics 365, will enable you to make an immediate impact. Why join us? At the University of Sunderland, we’re more than a place of learning, we’re a welcoming community that values inclusivity, collaboration, and well-being. We don’t just offer jobs, we offer careers that come with support, flexibility, and plenty of perks: Up to 49 days’ holiday - that’s 36 days’ annual leave, 5 festive closure days and 8 Bank Holidays! Award-winning staff networks that celebrate who you are. Lifestyle benefits, with savings on shopping, tech, bikes, and even cars. Health and well-being support, from private medical cover to gym discounts. Learning and development that helps you achieve your goals. Ready to Apply? Before getting started, please download the Role Profile under ‘Job Description’ so you have everything you need. Our application questions assess you directly against the essential and desirable criteria for the role. We do not review CVs at this stage, so please provide detailed, evidence-based answers to help us understand your suitability. Closing date: Sunday 6th September (23:59 GMT) Email details to a friend Apply Online Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Department Technical Services - Security, Compliance & Transformation Location Sunderland Campus Salary £38,786 to £46,049 Hours per Week 37 Closing Date Sunday 06 September 2026 Interview Date To be confirmed Reference 0315-26 Apply Online Current Vacancies Sunderland Vacancies Graduate Internships London Vacancies Overseas Vacancies Partner Organisations Student/Graduate Opportunities Find Jobs Jobs by Email Search Jobs: Search Advanced Search Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookie Information | Accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.sunderland.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=0286-26": {
      "title": "Content Creator (Intern)",
      "description": "0286-26 Content Creator (Intern) - Jobs at the University of Sunderland Skip to main content University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Terms of Use Contact Us Cookie Information Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Content Creator (Intern) Go to The University of Sunderland Close menu University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Close Search Search Search Further details: Job Description Proud to be Sunderland The University of Sunderland offers life‑changing opportunities for more than 27,500 students across our campuses in Sunderland, London and Hong Kong, as well as through global partnerships in 19 countries. We’re an inclusive, ambitious and forward‑looking University in a vibrant city that’s constantly evolving. We’re also entering an exciting new phase with a refreshed vision and strategic ambitions shaped around the changing higher education landscape. As we move through 2026, we’re celebrating being recognised as: A top 30 UK university (Guardian University Guide 2026) 1st in the North ‑ East for student support services (Daily Mail University Guide 2026) 1st in the North ‑ East for teaching quality (The Times & Sunday Times Good University Guide 2026) Your next opportunity Join our External Relations team as a Content Creator Intern and help bring the University of Sunderland story to life across our digital channels. This is an exciting opportunity to gain hands-on experience creating engaging content for social media, web and multimedia platforms while working alongside experienced marketing and communications professionals. From producing videos and podcasts to capturing student stories and supporting major campaigns, you'll play a key role in showcasing our vibrant community and inspiring future students. You'll have the chance to develop your creative skills, explore emerging digital trends, and build a portfolio of content that makes a real impact. Is this you? You're a creative and enthusiastic content creator who loves bringing ideas to life through social media, video and digital storytelling. Comfortable experimenting with new trends and platforms, you enjoy creating content that connects with different audiences and sparks engagement. You'll be confident working collaboratively with colleagues, organised in managing multiple priorities, and happy stepping in front of the camera to present content such as podcasts, vox pops and video features. Most importantly, you're keen to learn, contribute fresh ideas, and help showcase everything that makes the University of Sunderland a fantastic place to study and work. Why join us? At the University of Sunderland, we’re more than a place of learning, we’re a welcoming community that values inclusivity, collaboration, and well-being. We don’t just offer jobs, we offer careers that come with support, flexibility, and plenty of perks: Up to 44 days’ holiday - that’s 31 days’ annual leave, 5 festive closure days and 8 Bank Holidays! Award-winning staff networks that celebrate who you are. Lifestyle benefits , with savings on shopping, tech, bikes, and even cars. Health and well-being support , from private medical cover to gym discounts. Learning and development that helps you achieve your goals. Ready to Apply? Before getting started, please download the Role Profile under ‘Job Description’ so you have everything you need. Our application questions assess you directly against the essential and desirable criteria for the role. We do not review CVs at this stage, so please provide detailed, evidence-based answers to help us understand your suitability. Closing date: Friday 4th September 2026 (23:59 GMT) If you have questions about the role, please contact: Matt Smith at matt.smith-1@sunderland.ac.uk or on 07771 359179 We may close this vacancy earlier than the advertised closing date if we receive a high volume of applications. If this sounds like the opportunity for you, don't wait – get your application in early! Email details to a friend Apply Online Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Department External Relations - Content & Web Location Sunderland Campus Salary £25,540 to £27,276\n              per annum Fixed Term (2 years) Hours per Week 37 Closing Date Friday 04 September 2026 Interview Date To be confirmed Reference 0286-26 Apply Online Current Vacancies Sunderland Vacancies Graduate Internships London Vacancies Overseas Vacancies Partner Organisations Student/Graduate Opportunities Find Jobs Jobs by Email Search Jobs: Search Advanced Search Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookie Information | Accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.sunderland.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=0275-26-R": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer in Sport and Exercise Physiology",
      "description": "0275-26-R Senior Lecturer in Sport and Exercise Physiology - Jobs at the University of Sunderland Skip to main content University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Terms of Use Contact Us Cookie Information Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Senior Lecturer in Sport and Exercise Physiology Go to The University of Sunderland Close menu University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Close Search Search Search Further details: Job Description Proud to be Sunderland The University of Sunderland offers life‑changing opportunities for more than 27,500 students across our campuses in Sunderland, London and Hong Kong, as well as through global partnerships in 19 countries. We’re an inclusive, ambitious and forward‑looking University in a vibrant city that’s constantly evolving. We’re also entering an exciting new phase with a refreshed vision and strategic ambitions shaped around the changing higher education landscape. As we move through 2026, we’re celebrating being recognised as: A top 30 UK university (Guardian University Guide 2026) 1st in the North ‑ East for student support services (Daily Mail University Guide 2026) 1st in the North ‑ East for teaching quality (The Times & Sunday Times Good University Guide 2026) Your next opportunity This is an exciting opportunity to be involved in the education of Sport and Exercise Science, and future Sport and Exercise Medicine practitioners in the vibrant School of Medicine, and to contribute to the promotion of teaching, research and reach-out activities across the School, and wider Faculty. You will join our creative team of educators and contribute to our thriving partnership with schools, colleges, sport, fitness, public health, and healthcare providers. We are seeking an experienced sport and exercise physiologist, preferably with an interest in clinical exercise physiology or sport and exercise medicine, with a passion for education and supporting the students undergoing professional development. Due to exciting new developments, there is an opportunity for an experienced educator to join the team on a two-year fixed term contract . Is this you? The successful candidate will ideally hold current professional membership with the Chartered Association of Sport and Exercise Sciences (CASES) or Clinical Exercise Physiology UK, and a PhD/Doctorate in a relevant subject area. Individual CASES Sport and Exercise Accreditation is desirable. Key experience and skills we are looking for include: o Significant experience leading and managing undergraduate and/or postgraduate courses. o Significant teaching experience in the fields of exercise physiology, clinical exercise physiology, or sport and exercise medicine, and research methods and applied professional practice are essential. A willingness to contribute to teaching biomechanics or performance analysis is desirable. o Significant experience providing outstanding personalised student/learner academic support and applied professional practice supervision. o Significant experience leading innovative programme developments in the higher education sector. o established regional, national, and/or international collaborations and networks in the field of sport and exercise physiology, clinical exercise physiology, and/or sport and exercise medicine to drive and strengthen innovation, research, and knowledge exchange. o established research profile along with significant experience leading high-impact research and building research capacity. The role requires the successful candidate to be an autonomous practitioner who can offer expert knowledge, guidance and support to the student and the wider team. This Senior Lecturer post is both exciting and challenging and requires excellent knowledge and understanding of teaching and learning; supporting staff and students within and across teams while successfully leading modules in an HEI setting. Why join us? At the University of Sunderland, we’re more than a place of learning, we’re a welcoming community that values inclusivity, collaboration, and well-being. We don’t just offer jobs, we offer careers that come with support, flexibility, and plenty of perks: Up to 49 days’ holiday - that’s 36 days’ annual leave, 5 festive closure days and 8 Bank Holidays! Award-winning staff networks that celebrate who you are. Lifestyle benefits , with savings on shopping, tech, bikes, and even cars. Health and well-being support , from private medical cover to gym discounts. Learning and development that helps you achieve your goals. Ready to Apply? Before getting started, please download the Role Profile under ‘Job Description’ so you have everything you need. Our application questions assess you directly against the essential and desirable criteria for the role. We do not review CVs at this stage, so please provide detailed, evidence-based answers to help us understand your suitability. Closing date: Friday 4th September (23:59 GMT) If you have questions about the role, please contact: Lisa.board@sunderland.ac.uk , (Associate Head of School, Sport, Health and Performance) or Will.evans@sunderland.ac.uk (Programme Lead). Email details to a friend Apply Online Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Department Health Sciences & Wellbeing - School of Medicine Location Sunderland Campus Salary £46,756 to £58,228 Hours per Week 37 Closing Date Friday 04 September 2026 Interview Date Wednesday 16 September 2026 Reference 0275-26-R Apply Online Current Vacancies Sunderland Vacancies Graduate Internships London Vacancies Overseas Vacancies Partner Organisations Student/Graduate Opportunities Find Jobs Jobs by Email Search Jobs: Search Advanced Search Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookie Information | Accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.sunderland.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=0294-26": {
      "title": "Assessment, Regulations and Progression Administrator",
      "description": "0294-26 Assessment, Regulations and Progression Administrator - Jobs at the University of Sunderland Skip to main content University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Terms of Use Contact Us Cookie Information Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Assessment, Regulations and Progression Administrator Go to The University of Sunderland Close menu University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Close Search Search Search Please note: this vacancy is only available to current employees of the University Further details: Job Description Proud to be Sunderland The University of Sunderland offers life‑changing opportunities for more than 27,500 students across our campuses in Sunderland, London and Hong Kong, as well as through global partnerships in 19 countries. We’re an inclusive, ambitious and forward‑looking University in a vibrant city that’s constantly evolving. We’re also entering an exciting new phase with a refreshed vision and strategic ambitions shaped around the changing higher education landscape. As we move through 2026, we’re celebrating being recognised as: A top 30 UK university (Guardian University Guide 2026) 1st in the North ‑ East for student support services (Daily Mail University Guide 2026) 1st in the North ‑ East for teaching quality (The Times & Sunday Times Good University Guide 2026) Your next opportunity Join a team that plays a vital role in supporting the student journey at the University of Sunderland. In this varied and rewarding position, you'll help ensure key academic processes run smoothly, contributing to an excellent experience for students and colleagues across the University. Working within a collaborative and supportive environment, you'll have the opportunity to build your skills, develop your expertise, and make a meaningful impact through the delivery of high-quality administrative services. Whether you're supporting important annual activities, working with colleagues across the institution, or helping to improve processes, you'll be part of a team that values professionalism, accuracy, and continuous improvement. Is this you? You're organised, proactive, and enjoy delivering great service to others. You take pride in working accurately, managing priorities effectively, and building positive relationships with a wide range of people. Comfortable using digital systems and adapting to new situations, you're keen to learn, develop, and contribute to a team-focused environment. Most importantly, you're someone who values collaboration, embraces continuous improvement, and wants to play a part in supporting student success. Why join us? At the University of Sunderland, we’re more than a place of learning, we’re a welcoming community that values inclusivity, collaboration, and well-being. We don’t just offer jobs, we offer careers that come with support, flexibility, and plenty of perks: Up to 44 days’ holiday - that’s 31 days’ annual leave, 5 festive closure days and 8 Bank Holidays! Award-winning staff networks that celebrate who you are. Lifestyle benefits , with savings on shopping, tech, bikes, and even cars. Health and well-being support , from private medical cover to gym discounts. Learning and development that helps you achieve your goals. Ready to Apply? Before getting started, please download the Role Profile under ‘Job Description’ so you have everything you need. Our application questions assess you directly against the essential and desirable criteria for the role. We do not review CVs at this stage, so please provide detailed, evidence-based answers to help us understand your suitability. Closing date: Thursday 3rd September 2026 (23:59 GMT) If you have questions about the role, please contact: Joanne White, Assessment Regulations and Progression Manager, on joanne.white@sunderland.ac.uk . We may close this vacancy earlier than the advertised closing date if we receive a high volume of applications. If this sounds like the opportunity for you, don't wait – get your application in early! Email details to a friend Apply Online View All Vacancies Job Details Department Academic Registry & Governance - Assessment, Regulations & Progression Location Sunderland Campus Salary £25,540 to £27,276 Hours per Week 37 Closing Date Thursday 03 September 2026 Interview Date To be confirmed Reference 0294-26 Apply Online Current Vacancies Sunderland Vacancies Graduate Internships London Vacancies Overseas Vacancies Partner Organisations Student/Graduate Opportunities Find Jobs Jobs by Email Search Jobs: Search Advanced Search Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookie Information | Accessibility"
