    "https://jobs.sunderland.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=0290-26": {
      "title": "Assessment, Regulations and Progression Senior Administrator",
      "description": "0290-26 Assessment, Regulations and Progression Senior Administrator - Jobs at the University of Sunderland Skip to main content University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Terms of Use Contact Us Cookie Information Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Assessment, Regulations and Progression Senior Administrator Go to The University of Sunderland Close menu University Home Careers Home Current Vacancies Our University Our Executive/Board Our People Our Place What We Do How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Close Search Search Search Please note: this vacancy is only available to current employees of the University Further details: Job Description Proud to be Sunderland The University of Sunderland offers life‑changing opportunities for more than 27,500 students across our campuses in Sunderland, London and Hong Kong, as well as through global partnerships in 19 countries. We’re an inclusive, ambitious and forward‑looking University in a vibrant city that’s constantly evolving. We’re also entering an exciting new phase with a refreshed vision and strategic ambitions shaped around the changing higher education landscape. As we move through 2026, we’re celebrating being recognised as: A top 30 UK university (Guardian University Guide 2026) 1st in the North ‑ East for student support services (Daily Mail University Guide 2026) 1st in the North ‑ East for teaching quality (The Times & Sunday Times Good University Guide 2026) Your next opportunity Join a key team at the heart of the student experience, where your expertise will help ensure the smooth delivery of essential academic processes across the University. As an experienced administrator, you'll have the opportunity to take ownership of complex activities, contribute to service improvements and work closely with colleagues across faculties and professional services. This is a role where your ideas and insight will be valued, offering the chance to make a visible impact while continuing to develop your professional skills within a supportive, collaborative environment. Please note, we are recruiting to 2 posts: 1 x Permanent 1 x Fixed-term (12 months) Is this you? You're a confident and organised professional who enjoys taking responsibility, solving problems and finding better ways of working. You build positive relationships with ease, communicate effectively with a range of stakeholders and remain focused on quality, even when managing competing priorities. Proactive and adaptable, you're keen to share your knowledge, support colleagues and contribute to a culture of continuous improvement. If you thrive in a collaborative environment and take pride in delivering excellent service, we'd love to hear from you. Why join us? At the University of Sunderland, we’re more than a place of learning, we’re a welcoming community that values inclusivity, collaboration, and well-being. We don’t just offer jobs, we offer careers that come with support, flexibility, and plenty of perks: Up to 44 days’ holiday - that’s 31 days’ annual leave, 5 festive closure days and 8 Bank Holidays! Award-winning staff networks that celebrate who you are. Lifestyle benefits , with savings on shopping, tech, bikes, and even cars. Health and well-being support , from private medical cover to gym discounts. Learning and development that helps you achieve your goals. Ready to Apply? Before getting started, please download the Role Profile under ‘Job Description’ so you have everything you need. Our application questions assess you directly against the essential and desirable criteria for the role. We do not review CVs at this stage, so please provide detailed, evidence-based answers to help us understand your suitability. Closing date: Thursday 3rd September 2026 (23:59 GMT) If you have questions about the role, please contact: Joanne White, Assessment Regulations and Progression Manager, on joanne.white@sunderland.ac.uk . We may close this vacancy earlier than the advertised closing date if we receive a high volume of applications. If this sounds like the opportunity for you, don't wait – get your application in early! Email details to a friend Apply Online View All Vacancies Job Details Department Academic Registry & Governance - Assessment, Regulations & Progression Location Sunderland Campus Salary £27,855 to £30,343 Hours per Week 37 Closing Date Thursday 03 September 2026 Interview Date To be confirmed Reference 0290-26 Apply Online Current Vacancies Sunderland Vacancies Graduate Internships London Vacancies Overseas Vacancies Partner Organisations Student/Graduate Opportunities Find Jobs Jobs by Email Search Jobs: Search Advanced Search Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookie Information | Accessibility"
    },
